    {
      "id": "04-carbs",
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "carbs",
      "text": "27.6 grams of carbs. Fibre is 10.3 grams, helping digestion and slowing the absorption of the other carbs. Starch is only 1.4 grams, but nuts are not supposed to be starch-based energy foods. The glycemic index is 30, meaning these carbs raise blood glucose relatively slowly. For nuts, fibre and glycemic behaviour matter far more than starch.",
      "textSha256": "bf1072220fb85a3fa73afdb4c88476b4b05eaee265b0641f440b7159e6ff9c1a",
